From: Abdelhafid DJIDEL <266947999+hafid-logic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:31:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(core): pin balanced virtual parent and group identity

### What
Pins `balanced_identity_result`: `getpid`/`getpgrp` report the virtual pid, `getppid` reports 1, the uid/gid family reports 0, and an unknown syscall reports `None`.

### Why it matters
The balanced contract virtualizes identity. The existing tests check the uid result and the mediated tid but not the parent/group arms, so deleting either arm survives the suite.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| delete `SYS_GETPPID => Some(1)` arm | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| delete `SYS_GETPGRP => Some(VIRTUAL_PID)` arm | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline (clean tree + new test): PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-core --lib balanced_identity`.

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs b/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs
index 5f87a3a..220f650 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs
@@ -934,4 +934,19 @@ mod tests {
             }
         }
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn balanced_identity_reports_virtual_parent_and_group() {
+        assert_eq!(
+            balanced_identity_result(SYS_GETPID),
+            Some(BALANCED_VIRTUAL_PID)
+        );
+        assert_eq!(balanced_identity_result(SYS_GETPPID), Some(1));
+        assert_eq!(
+            balanced_identity_result(SYS_GETPGRP),
+            Some(BALANCED_VIRTUAL_PID)
+        );
+        assert_eq!(balanced_identity_result(SYS_GETUID), Some(0));
+        assert_eq!(balanced_identity_result(999), None);
+    }
 }
